SUMMARY:Ask Haislet to check the estate account for TC 421 <2026-10-08 Thu>
DESCRIPTION:*Decision 2026-09-27: go through Haislet\, not a 4506-T.* The t
 rust\nneeds all three trustees to act\, so the trustee route means Lisa an
 d\nRebecca sign too. The "Executor" title needs court letters\, and there\
 nwas no probate.  Final 706 p.2 names G. Scott Haislet as the estate's\nre
 presentative\, with authority to receive confidential tax info\n(Reg. 601.
 504(b)(2)(i)).\n• Contact: scott@goscott.com\, cc marianne@goscott.com /\n
   tax@goscott.com\; office 925-283-1031.\n• Ask: check the 706 account (Br
 enda's SSN\, DOD 02/12/2025) for TC\n  421\, by phone on the estate & gift
  line (866-699-4083) or by TDS if\n  he has a 2848 on file. 706 filed 2026
 -04-08\; IRS says wait 6 months\n  (9 for TDS).\n• Fallback: the 4506-T pa
 cket below (4506T-*.pdf\, excluded from git).\nBrenda's Form 706 was maile
 d by Haislet's office 2026-04-08.  IRS says\nwait 6 months after filing be
 fore requesting an account transcript.\nTC 421 on the transcript = return 
 accepted as filed / exam complete\n(functional equivalent of the closing l
 etter\, which is no longer sent\nautomatically).  If no TC 421 yet\, check
  again later. Closing letter\n(optional\, $67 via Pay.gov) can be requeste
 d 9 months after filing\n(~Jan 2027) or any time once TC 421 appears.\n\nC
 an do this myself (signed the 706 as executor — no need to involve\nHaisle
 t): Form 4506-T: <https://www.irs.gov/pub/irs-pdf/f4506t.pdf>\n• Line 1a: 
 Estate of Brenda A. Webster\n• Line 1b: Brenda's SSN (NOT the estate EIN —
  706 account is keyed to\n  decedent SSN)\n• Line 3: my name\, title "Exec
 utor"\, address — must match what's on\n  the filed 706\n• Line 6: 706\, c
 heck box 6b (Account Transcript) — only valid option\n  for estate tax\n• 
 Line 9: period = date-of-death year-end\n• Check attestation box\, sign\, 
 date\, Title line = "Executor" (else\n  rejected)\n• Send to Ogden UT RAIV
 S team (CA domicile) — fax faster than mail\,\n  use fax number from the c
 hart in the current form's instructions\n• Transcript arrives by mail in a
  few weeks\; look for TC 421 in\n  transaction list\nPhone status check: I
 RS estate & gift tax line 866-699-4083 Ref:\n<https://www.irs.gov/business
 es/small-businesses-self-employed/transcripts-in-lieu-of-estate-tax-closin
 g-letters>\n\n*Corrections from IRS page\, checked 2026-09-27* (supersede 
 the list\n above):\n• Line 9 = *date of death* 02/12/2025\, not year-end.\
 n• No probate\, trust-administered: Title = "Trustee of the Brenda\n  Webs
 ter Living Trust dated April 9\, 1998" (not "Executor"). Attach\n  (a) a s
 igned statement that no probate will be commenced and (b) a\n  Certificate
  of Trust or the full trust instrument. Without these it\n  gets rejected.
 \n• IRS says wait 6 months after filing for 4506-T (9 months for the TDS\n
   route). The 6 months ends 10-08\; don't fax before then.\n• Fax: Ogden R
 AIVS\, 855-298-1145 ("all other transcripts" chart\, CA).\n• Pre-filled fo
 rm:\n  <file:office/4506T-estate-brenda-webster-DRAFT.pdf>.  Still to fill
 :\n  1b SSN\, phone\, attestation box\, signature\, date.  Line 3 now matc
 hes\n  the final 706 (Desktop/Scott Haislet-1771726762833): sole executor\
 n  "Michael Webster"\, 1942 N. Alvarado Street\, LA 90039.  Phone (323)\n 
  352-4260 (matches 706).  Paperless has no Living Trust\n  certification\;
  the 2023 BNY certs are for the 1937 Schwabacher FBO\n  Brenda trust.\n• A
 ttachments: <file:office/4506T-no-probate-statement.pdf> (Michael\n  signs
 ) and <file:office/4506T-certification-of-trust.pdf> (all 3\n  trustees si
 gn\; the bracketed blanks must be filled from the trust\n  instrument). Or
  ask Matthew Talbot for the one on file\, or attach\n  the full trust + am
 endments.
CATEGORIES:cal,estate,org-calendar-staging
END:VEVENT
